# MAIN Cursor Instructions: PHYTO.bg WordPress Catalog Project

Read this file first. It is the router/index for the project rule set.

## Project in one sentence

Build a Bulgarian WordPress catalog/information site based on the PHYTO reference/design, using a custom classic theme, ACF, custom post types, plain CSS, and no e-commerce or public customer-auth features.

## Non-negotiable scope

Do not build:

- WooCommerce.
- Cart.
- Checkout.
- Buy buttons.
- Add-to-cart.
- Prices/payment/shipping/order logic.
- Stock/inventory logic.
- Public login/register/account pages.
- Wishlist/order history/customer dashboard.
- Public users/auth.
- Quiz module.

WordPress admin users are allowed only for content management.

## Rule priority

When rules overlap, follow this order:

1. `000-main-phyto-cursor-instructions.mdc`
   - This router/index file.
   - Use first to decide which supporting rule files apply.

2. `selecta-phyto-catalog-project-context.mdc`
   - Project scope and business rules.
   - Use for all decisions about what the site is and is not.
   - This file overrides generic WordPress examples.

3. `selecta-phyto-sitemap-context.mdc`
   - Reference-site structure and route/template mapping.
   - Use when building navigation, pages, product archives, product detail pages, advice/blog pages, CMS pages, legal pages, partners/store locator, and footer structure.

4. `selecta-figma-mcp-wordpress-instructions.mdc`
   - Figma MCP workflow.
   - Use whenever implementing UI from Figma frames/components.
   - Figma is the visual source of truth; WordPress/ACF/CPT rules are the architecture source of truth.

5. `wordpress-acf-theme-instructions-updated.mdc`
   - General always-on WordPress custom theme rules.
   - Use for PHP, template hierarchy, asset loading, ACF safety, CPTs, escaping, security, and plain CSS practices.

6. `wordpress-acf-theme-skill-updated.mdc`
   - Detailed implementation skill.
   - Use when planning/building/refactoring components, templates, CPTs, ACF fields, product catalog pages, advice pages, and CSS.

## Which file to use when

Use `selecta-phyto-catalog-project-context.mdc` when the task asks about:

- project scope
- catalog-only behavior
- what to remove from the reference site
- no e-commerce
- no public auth
- product CPT strategy
- brand reuse
- global components
- tracking/GDPR/newsletter boundaries

Use `selecta-phyto-sitemap-context.mdc` when the task asks about:

- site map
- routes
- page structure
- navigation
- mega menu
- homepage sections
- product listing pages
- product detail pages
- advice/blog
- CMS pages
- legal/footer pages
- partners/store locator

Use `selecta-figma-mcp-wordpress-instructions.mdc` when the task asks about:

- Figma
- Figma MCP
- implementing a Figma frame
- mapping design to code
- extracting CSS variables
- assets/icons/images from Figma
